      "id": "g_noun_gender_article",
      "grammar": true,
      "english": "the milk (feminine noun → la)",
      "word": "la leche",
      "grammarNote": "Every Spanish noun is masculine or feminine, and the article agrees:\n**el** (masc.) · **la** (fem.) → **el pan** (bread), **la leche** (milk). Most **-o** words are masculine, most **-a** feminine — but learn each noun with its article.",
      "englishPhrase": "The bread is here, the milk is there.",
      "phrase": "El pan está aquí, la leche está allí.",
      "literal": [
        [
          "El",
          "the"
        ],
        [
          "pan",
          "bread"
        ],
        [
          "la",
          "the"
        ],
        [
          "leche",
          "milk"
        ]
      ],
      "format": "table",
      "table": {
        "title": "Definite articles agree with gender & number",
        "rows": [
          [
            "masc. sing.",
            "el (el pan)"
          ],
          [
            "fem. sing.",
            "la (la leche)"
          ],
          [
            "masc. pl.",
            "los (los libros)"
          ],
          [
            "fem. pl.",
            "las (las casas)"
          ]
        ],
        "note": "Most -o words are masculine, most -a feminine — learn each noun with its article."
      }
    },
